public Set<V> intersection(Set<V> set1, Set<V> set2) {
    return Stream.of(set1, set2).flatMap(Collection::stream).collect(Collectors.toSet());
}
```
This code uses the `Stream` API to create a stream from each set and then uses the `flatMap` method to flatten the stream of streams into a single stream, which is then collected into a set using the `Collectors.toSet()` method. This code is more efficient than the previous code because it avoids iterating over both sets twice, as the `flatMap` method only iterates over each element of the outer stream once.

/**
 * Efficient way to compute the intersection between two sets
 *
 * @param set1 set $1$
 * @param set2 set $2$
 * @return intersection of set $1$ and $2$
 */
private Set<V> intersection(Set<V> set1, Set<V> set2) {
    return set1.stream()
            .filter(set2::contains)
            .collect(Collectors.toSet());
}

